Practical 1: Photoshop Interface and Basic Tools
Step-by-Step Procedure

1 File > New. Set Width 1200 px, Height 800 px, Resolution 72 ppi, RGB. Click Create.

2 Tour the workspace: Toolbar (left), Options Bar (top), Layers panel and Properties (right), Menu Bar (very top). Take a screenshot with them labelled.

3 Pick the Rectangle, Ellipse and Polygon shape tools and draw 3 shapes, using at least 2 different fill colors.

4 Try the Move (V), Rectangular Marquee (M), Lasso (L), Brush (B), Eraser (E) and Crop (C) tools. Do a

small edit with each so you can describe it.

5 Select the Type tool (T) and type: Your Name, Roll No, Course (Desktop Publishing - UAC012P).

6 File > Save As > Photoshop (.psd). Then File > Export > Export As > JPG.
Practical 2: Photo Editing and Basic Retouching

Module 1

Objective: To perform basic photo editing and retouching using Adobe Photoshop.

Task Requirements

Select an ordinary photograph and open it in Photoshop.

Crop and straighten the image.

Adjust Brightness/Contrast.

Correct basic Color Balance/Saturation.

Remove at least three unwanted spots or objects using suitable retouching tools.

Use Healing Brush, Spot Healing Brush, or Clone Stamp where appropriate.

Prepare Before and After versions.

Save the PSD and export the final image.

Step-by-Step Procedure

1 Open your own photo (File > Open). Duplicate the background layer (Ctrl+J) and keep the original for the Before shot.

2 Use the Crop tool (C); use the Straighten option to level the horizon, then press Enter.

3 Image > Adjustments > Brightness/Contrast; adjust modestly.

4 Image > Adjustments > Color Balance and Hue/Saturation for basic color correction.

5 Remove 3 blemishes or objects with the Spot Healing Brush (J) or Clone Stamp (S, Alt-click to sample).

6 Place Before and After side by side on a new canvas and export as Before_After_Practical_02.jpg.

7 Save PSD and export the final JPG. 



Practical 3: Layers, Masks and Creative Composition

Module 2

Objective: To understand layers and layer masks by creating a composite image.

Task Requirements

Create a creative travel poster/composite image using at least three photographs.

Place each image on a separate layer and rename layers appropriately.

Use Layer Masks to blend or remove portions of images.

Use Move and Transform options to adjust image placement.

Add a suitable background.

Add a title and supporting text.

Apply at least one Layer Style such as Drop Shadow, Stroke, or Outer Glow.

Save the PSD and export the final composition.

Step-by-Step Procedure

1 Create a new document and fill a background (gradient or sky color).

2 Place 3 or more travel photos (File > Place Embedded). Rename each layer (e.g. Mountain, Beach, City).

3 Select a layer, click Add Layer Mask, and paint with a black soft brush to hide edges and blend photos smoothly.

4 Use Ctrl+T (Free Transform) to resize and position each photo.

5 Add a title such as 'Explore the World and supporting text with the Type tool.

6 Add a Layer Style (fx button): Drop Shadow, Stroke or Outer Glow on the title.

7 Save PSD, export JPG.

